I recently had the privilege of attending the Australia-India Strategic Technology Collaboration event at Taj, Bengaluru, and as an aspiring tech entrepreneur, the experience was nothing short of electric!

@AusCGBengaluru 
@Austrade 
@AustradeIndia 
@dfat 
@AusIndiaCentre 
@AIBC_National 

It was an incredible reminder of just how expansive and welcoming the tech ecosystem truly is. 

For me - being in an environment buzzing with bilateral innovation isn't just motivating; it’s a masterclass in what happens when cross-border synergy is put into action.

What stood out most wasn't just the caliber of the discussions around emerging tech, AI, and digital transformation, but the accessibility of the people driving them:

• Visionary Leaders & Established Pioneers: Hearing firsthand from seasoned founders and industry veterans who have scaled solutions across global markets offered a grounded perspective on resilience, execution, and building for long-term impact.

• Diplomats & Policy Shapers: Connecting with diplomatic representatives highlighted the strategic bridge being built between Australia and India. Seeing how policy and international partnerships are actively clearing the runway for cross-border startups gives immense confidence to builders looking at global horizons.

• Trailblazing Women in Tech: The energy, insights, and leadership brought to the table by women in tech were a major highlight- challenging conventional playbooks and setting a high bar for inclusive innovation.

• Driven Industry Peers: Exchanging ideas with fellow builders, technologists, and innovators reinforced a simple truth: the best breakthroughs happen when sharp minds share notes openly rather than working in silos.

Walking away from these conversations, one thing is clear - the Australia-India tech corridor is wide open for bold ideas and meaningful collaboration. Grateful for the connections made, the wisdom shared, and the renewed fuel to keep building.

Onward and upward from here. 🚀

