So I offered to pay for your roadside assistance to take the vehicle to the service centre. No slot for that either.
If I had broken down in the middle of the road, what was I supposed to do? For people who rely on a two-wheeler for their daily commute, this isn't an inconvenience. It disrupts our whole day.
Consumer forums and regulators need to take note. A company that can't service the vehicles already on the road shouldn't be pushing more sales. Fix service first.
